WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:13.833
This guideline is about text fields specifically: showing the user any particular characteristics the text they type should have. For example, if I want them to write a password and there

2
00:00:13.833 --> 00:00:25.167
are specific instructions it must follow, like having at least one capital letter, a special character, and so on, I need to show that before they start typing. I shouldn't let

3
00:00:25.167 --> 00:00:36.500
them type and then tell them there's an error, that they shouldn't have done that. The requirements or instructions they need to follow should always be visible while they enter the input.

4
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:48.500
Also, we often find a Clear or Reset button in some forms that lets me wipe all the data I've typed. This button is very, very rarely used, and often when it's there it gets pressed by mistake.

5
00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:06.167
We don't usually use Reset or Clear buttons; they aren't used much. If in some forms we know users enter private and very important data, and they may need,

6
00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:15.833
if they want to go back, to cancel, wipe it and make sure the data they typed has been deleted, then we can give them a Cancel button, so they're

7
00:01:15.833 --> 00:01:25.500
sure that pressing it removes everything they typed. But we give that Cancel button a lower hierarchy than the button that lets them continue or go to the next step.

8
00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:35.945
Finally, the last guideline about forms and text fields: showing the user the error that happened. If an error happens, we make it very clear and specific, like this example: we

9
00:01:35.945 --> 00:01:46.390
can write the error itself in red text, add an icon to show the error is here, and make the border red too, to show there's an error. The message itself

10
00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:56.835
needs to be clear and explain what error they made. This reminds us, if we go back to the usability heuristics, of the heuristic about helping users recognize and diagnose the

11
00:01:56.835 --> 00:02:07.280
error they made: here I show them where the error is in the first place, and explain through this message exactly what error they made, so they can also recover from it.
